 for Cloud-Native Microservices", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23778983", "publication_date": "2026-10-30", "description": "<p><strong>Replication package for &ldquo;From Anomaly Detection to Cause-Aware Response: Counterfactual Resilience Control for Cloud-Native Microservices&rdquo; &mdash; Version 4.2</strong></p>\n<p>This record provides the complete synthetic-data replication package supporting the study <em>From Anomaly Detection to Cause-Aware Response: Counterfactual Resilience Control for Cloud-Native Microservices</em>. It incorporates the original ten-master-seed benchmark in full (12,200 synthetic episode specifications, including NORMAL reference episodes, and 109,800 candidate-action outcomes), together with the code, inputs, stored results, and verification tools for all subsequent analyses reported in the revised manuscript. Users do not need a separate download of the earlier benchmark version.</p>\n<p>The archive contains the original simulator and evaluation pipeline, an independent sampled replay (M1), matched-action comparisons (M2), actuator-selectivity experiments including 23,700 additional synthetic simulator rollouts (M3), graph reachability and physical-fault diagnostics (M4), classifier-error and action-regret analyses (M5), and cause-aware versus cause-agnostic loss decomposition with subgroup analyses (M6).</p>\n<p>It also includes supplementary tables S1, S2, S2b, and S3, all seven vector figures, pinned Python dependencies, a manuscript-to-evidence map, reproducibility instructions, validation scripts, a complete SHA-256 file manifest, and a version changelog.</p>\n<p>All measurements and outcomes are generated in an abstract simulated microservice environment. No deployed Kubernetes cluster, production telemetry, or field-effectiveness assessment is included. Model comparisons and subgroup analyses should be interpreted within the stated simulator assumptions. Secondary analyses are exploratory, and uncertainty is evaluated at the master-seed level.</p>\n<p>The archive contains stored reference results and executable scripts for independent verification and regeneration. A complete rerun of the more computationally intensive simulations may require substantial computing time.</p>\n<p><strong>Licensing:</strong> Author-owned software and executable configurations are provided under the MIT License. Author-owned synthetic data, numerical results, tables, figures, and scientific documentation are provided under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). The files <code>LICENSE.md</code>, <code>LICENSE-CODE</code>, and <code>LICENSE-DATA</code> specify the scope of each license.</p>\n<p><strong>Version-specific DOI:</strong> <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23778983\">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23778983</a></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bondaruk, Tymofii", "affiliation": "G.E. Pukhov Institute for Modelling in Energy Engineering of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine", "orcid": "0009-0000-8120-2787"}, {"name": "Shkarupylo, Vadym", "affiliation": "G.E. Pukhov Institute for Modelling in Energy Engineering of the National Academy of Sciences of Ukraine", "orcid": "0000-0002-0523-8910"}, {"name": "Artemchuk, Volodymyr", "affiliation": "G.E. Pukhov Institute for Modelling in Energy Engineering of NAS of Ukraine", "orcid": "0000-0001-8819-4564"}], "keywords": ["cloud-native resilience", "microservices", "cause-aware control", "counterfactual simulation", "autoscaling", "distributed denial of service", "root cause analysis", "self-healing systems", "uncertainty quantification"], "version": "4.2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22548161"}}]}}, "title": "Reproducibility package for From Anomaly Detection to Cause-Aware Response: Counterfactual Resilience Control for Cloud-Native Microservices", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23778983", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23778983?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23778983", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23778983", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23778983", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22548161", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22548161", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22548161", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22548161", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23778983/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23778983/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23778983/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-30T17:00:59.996338+00:00", "recid": "23778983", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "3eb36139-7544-45a6-9b08-e90b36e2ae26", "key": "Cloud_Microservices_Zenodo_v4.2_FINAL.zip", "size": 49895391, "checksum": "md5:5c2ac05f18ece2c5bb81ba3850bfecbc", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23778983/files/Cloud_Microservices_Zenodo_v4.2_FINAL.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "58925"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 5, "unique_downloads": 5, "views": 29, "unique_views": 28, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 2, "version_views": 2}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-30T14:43:38.560211+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-30T14:43:38.861865+00:00", "id": 23809273, "conceptrecid": "23809272", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23809272", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "metadata": {"title": "Computing replication package: Auditing Class Rebalancing and Decision Thresholds in Software Defect Prediction under Feature-Group Separation", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "publication_date": "2026-10-30", "description": "<p>This record contains the replication materials accompanying the manuscript &ldquo;Auditing Class Rebalancing and Decision Thresholds in Software Defect Prediction under Feature-Group Separation.&rdquo;</p>\n<p>The package provides the analysis code, aggregate and fold-level results, provenance manifests, experimental protocols, source transformations, saved verification outputs, and an independent verification script. The study evaluates five NASA PROMISE datasets and a deterministic external cohort of 18 Apache projects using logistic regression and random forest with no rebalancing, class weighting, and SMOTE under conventional and exact-feature-grouped evaluation.</p>\n<p>The package supports verification of fold-to-project aggregation, project-level contrasts, exact sign-flip tests, Holm corrections, and descriptive bootstrap intervals. The 18 external projects belong to a common Apache data lineage and are not treated as 18 independent organizations.</p>\n<p>Third-party NASA/PROMISE and IND-JLMIV+R raw feature tables, per-record labels and predictions, and exact feature-group identifiers are not redistributed. Therefore, this is an auditable compact evidence package rather than a complete end-to-end replay archive. Users should obtain third-party inputs from the cited sources and follow their original terms.</p>\n<p>Original code, aggregate evidence, manifests, protocols, and documentation are released under CC BY 4.0. Third-party materials retain their original terms.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Wang, Fengqi", "affiliation": "Hubei University"}], "keywords": ["software defect prediction", "class imbalance", "SMOTE", "decision threshold", "feature-group separation", "reproducibility", "empirical software engineering", "machine learning"], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23809272"}}]}}, "title": "Computing replication package: Auditing Class Rebalancing and Decision Thresholds in Software Defect Prediction under Feature-Group Separation", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23809273", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23809273", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23809273?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23809273", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23809273/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23809272", 